            "custom_liquid": "<style> .yc-faq { all: initial; display: block; background: #FFFFFF; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif; max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1rem; box-sizing: border-box; } .yc-faq *, .yc-faq *::before, .yc-faq *::after { box-sizing: border-box; font-family: inherit; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid #E4E0D8; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-item:first-child { border-top: 1px solid #E4E0D8; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-question { width: 100%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; text-align: left; padding: 1.2rem 0.25rem; font-size: 1.3rem; color: #2B2A28; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-question:hover { color: #55483a; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-icon { flex-shrink: 0; width: 18px; height: 18px; position: relative; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-icon::before, .yc-faq .yc-faq-icon::after { content: \"\"; position: absolute; background: #2B2A28; top: 50%; left: 50%; transition: transform 0.25s ease; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-icon::before { width: 100%; height: 2px; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); } .yc-faq .yc-faq-icon::after { width: 2px; height: 100%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); } .yc-faq .yc-faq-item.yc-open .yc-faq-icon::after { transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg); opacity: 0; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-answer { max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; transition: max-height 0.3s ease, padding 0.3s ease; font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #4a4640; padding: 0 0.25rem; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-item.yc-open .yc-faq-answer { max-height: 400px; padding: 0 0.25rem 1.2rem; } /* Mobile: keep text comfortably readable */ @media (max-width: 480px) { .yc-faq { padding: 0.75rem; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-question { font-size: 1.35rem; padding: 1.2rem 0.15rem; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-answer { font-size: 1.25rem; } .yc-faq .yc-faq-icon { width: 22px; height: 22px; } } </style> <div class=\"yc-faq\"> <div class=\"yc-faq-item\"> <button class=\"yc-faq-question\" type=\"button\"> How does it work? <span class=\"yc-faq-icon\"></span> </button> <div class=\"yc-faq-answer\"> The serum has PDRN and caffeine, two popular scalp care ingredients. The built-in brush spreads it right onto your scalp, so it goes where you need it. It feels cool and light, and it leaves no grease. </div> </div> <div class=\"yc-faq-item\"> <button class=\"yc-faq-question\" type=\"button\"> Is it safe to use? <span class=\"yc-faq-icon\"></span> </button> <div class=\"yc-faq-answer\"> It is made to be gentle on your scalp. Before your first use, test a small spot on your skin to be sure it feels okay. If you are pregnant, nursing, or have a skin problem, ask your doctor first. </div> </div> <div class=\"yc-faq-item\"> <button class=\"yc-faq-question\" type=\"button\"> How do I use it? <span class=\"yc-faq-icon\"></span> </button> <div class=\"yc-faq-answer\"> Part your hair and brush the serum along your scalp. Then gently rub it in with your fingertips. You do not need to rinse it out. </div> </div> <div class=\"yc-faq-item\"> <button class=\"yc-faq-question\" type=\"button\"> Can I use it with my other hair products? <span class=\"yc-faq-icon\"></span> </button> <div class=\"yc-faq-answer\"> Yes. Use it on a clean scalp, after you wash your hair. It fits easily into the routine you already have. </div> </div> </div> <script> (function () { var items = document.querySelectorAll('.yc-faq .yc-faq-item'); items.forEach(function (item) { var btn = item.querySelector('.yc-faq-question'); btn.addEventListener('click', function () { item.classList.toggle('yc-open'); }); }); })(); </script>"
